// TerrainTranscodeSnowOverrides.kdl
//
// Purpose:
// - Optional Classic Client -> Enhanced Client terrain transcode overlay for a
//   snow-biased map view.
// - Apply after `TerrainTranscode.kdl`; later `t` rows win for duplicate CC
//   land ids in the existing transcode loader.
// - This file is intentionally not the active default table. To use it today,
//   append these rows after the normal table content, or merge them into a
//   local copy of `TerrainTranscode.kdl`.
//
// Source:
// - UO Enhanced Map Converter 3.5 `_conversiontables/` transition files with
//   names ending in `TO...txt`.
// - Each EMC source CC land id is routed to the EC material slot currently used
//   by that EMC target CC land id in this repository's `TerrainTranscode.kdl`.
//
// Caveats:
// - EMC labels these as transition-table conversions, and the result is a
//   broad winterization pass rather than a fully reviewed material model.
// - A few EMC snow2dirt target CC ids currently resolve to generic dirt/rock
//   material slots here. Those mappings are preserved as target-slot evidence
//   instead of inventing unsupported snow transition material ids.

// Grass / forest base -> snow base.
t 8 3 4 5 6 196 197 198 199

// Forest-rock transition sources whose EMC targets resolve to snow base.
t 8 236 237 238 239 240 241 242 243

// Forest-dirt transition sources whose EMC targets resolve to snow base.
t 8 353 354 355 356 357 358 359 360

// Forest-dirt transition sources whose EMC targets currently resolve to dirt.
t 2 361 362 363 364

// Forest-rock transition sources whose EMC targets currently resolve to rock.
t 6 244 245 246 247

// Grass/forest water and cliff transition sources -> snow cliff/embank slots.
t 61 27 34 35 38 39 742 743 750 755 772
t 62 26 29 32 741 751 752 760 763
t 63 28 33 36 37 40 147 154 162 163 746 747 749 753 754 773
t 64 30 31 161 761 762
t 65 142 143 150 151 155
t 66 152 160
t 67 146 153

// EMC identity/questionable grass-water-dark rows retained as target-slot
// evidence because the targets resolve to the original non-snow slots.
t 58 141
t 59 149
t 60 145
